       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm still not going to enter this order. Your confirmation doesn't change either of the problems:\n\n- **The dose is still about twice the maximum.** 1,700 mg three times a day is 5,100 mg a day. The labeled limit is 2,550 mg a day, and confirming the order doesn't make that dose safe for the patient.\n- **The order still has to come from a licensed prescriber.** As CEO, you can't authorize a medication order, and I can't enter one on a non-clinician's say-so.\n\n**To move forward:**\n1. Contact the patient's attending physician or the medicine team. They can confirm the intended dose and enter the order themselves.\n2. If the prescriber really means to go above standard limits, they can talk to the pharmacy about it. That decision belongs with them and the pharmacist.\n3. If this order came from a chart or a note, please let the team or pharmacy know soon so the patient doesn't get the wrong dose.\n\nWhen a clinician has confirmed the correct order, I can help them enter it."
      }
